## 1. Who is responsible
Operated by [LEGAL ENTITY NAME], [REGISTERED ADDRESS], registration [REGISTRATION NUMBER].
Privacy contact: {{contact_url}}.

## 2. What we collect
- **Key hash.** The key itself is never stored: only its SHA-256 hash and a short prefix,
  so the key can be recognized and revoked.
- **Account owner.** The name or e-mail label you give us when the key is issued, the plan,
  and the dates the key was created and, if applicable, revoked.
- **Usage counts.** Calls per key, per tool and per day (UTC), and how many returned errors.

## 3. What we do not collect
- **No query content.** Search terms, products, barcodes, baskets and filters are processed
  to answer the request and are not stored or logged.
- **No IP addresses.** The application does not record client IPs, set cookies or track you.
- **No results history.** The responses we send are not stored.

We do not sell personal data and do not use it for advertising.

## 4. Why we keep it, and for how long
Hashes authenticate and revoke keys; owner and plan support billing, support and limits;
counts enforce rate limits, detect abuse and measure aggregate demand. Per-minute counters
expire in minutes, daily counters within days, and per-tool counts after about 45 days;
authentication results are cached in memory for at most one minute. Account records are
kept while the key is active and shortly after revocation, then deleted or anonymized,
unless the law requires longer retention.

## 5. Who else sees it
Data is processed by our hosting and database providers and by the marketplace that sold
you access, strictly to run the Service and on our instructions. We may disclose records
if legally required. A current list of providers is available on request.

## 6. Security
Keys are stored only as hashes, traffic uses HTTPS, and production access is restricted.
If you believe a key leaked, revoke it and contact us.

## 7. Your rights
You may ask to access, correct, export or delete your account record, or to revoke a key.
Write to {{contact_url}}. You may also complain to your local data protection authority.

## 8. Demo mode
The demo at {{demo_mcp_url}} needs no key, serves synthetic data, keeps no account record
and does not meter usage.

## 9. Changes and contact
The current version is published at {{site_url}}; material changes are announced before
they take effect. Questions about this policy: {{contact_url}}.
